  "title": "Canyon Runner",
  "date": "2025-06-03",
  "excerpt": "Designed to roam deep canyons and high plateaus, the Canyon Runner is a Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD conversion engineered for remote adventure and long-term off-grid living. Powered by 800Ah of lithium batteries, a 400W so",
  "body": [
    "Designed to roam deep canyons and high plateaus, the Canyon Runner is a Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD conversion engineered for remote adventure and long-term off-grid living. Powered by 800Ah of lithium batteries, a 400W solar array, and a 3000W inverter, this van delivers serious electrical autonomy—easily supporting Starlink internet, a Weboost signal booster, induction cooking, and full interior climate control. With 30amp shore power backup and a DC-DC charger, it’s ready for any charging setup, no matter how remote your travels take you.",
    "Inside, the van’s rugged utility is matched by modern craftsmanship. A full wet bath with a 36-inch wide tiled shower and outdoor rinse station ensures you stay clean no matter the dust level outside. The kitchen setup includes a double burner induction cooktop, undermount sink with stainless fixtures, and a fridge/freezer large enough for extended trips. Charcoal-stained butcher block countertops and espresso ceilings are balanced by painted shiplap walls and white cabinetry, creating a warm, tailored interior space built for full-time use.",
    "Adventure continues outside with an Agile RIP lift kit, CA Tuned front bumper, and all-terrain tires mounted on matte black Arsenal rims. The integrated roof rack, bike carrier system, exterior lighting package, and onboard ARB air compressor make this build ideal for off-roaders, cyclists, and overlanders alike. The electric awning with LED lighting offers shade and shelter wherever you land, while magnetic bug nets and blackout shades transform the cabin into a quiet refuge after a long day on the trail.",
    "Creature comforts haven’t been overlooked. A queen memory foam bed sits above dual heavy-duty pullout gear trays. A bench seat cleverly doubles as a dog bed with a sliding platform, and a swivel-mounted smart TV ensures you can unwind with a view of the desert stars or your favorite show. Whether you're chasing red rock sunsets or charting multi-day routes off the grid, the Canyon Runner was built to move with you, not behind you."
  ],
